Package: NeuralForest
Title: Adaptive Neural-Guided Random Forests
Version: 0.9.4
Authors@R: person("Quentin", "Lamboley", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "145555916+QuentinLamboley@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: A native C++17 random forest engine for classification and regression
    augmented by an out-of-bag neural difficulty learner and gradient-trained
    oblique soft decision trees. A neural network guides bootstrap sampling
    and feature selection while soft tree split projections and thresholds
    are differentiated with respect to metric-dependent surrogate losses.
    Includes distribution-aware presets, leakage-resistant preprocessing,
    ridge-regularized linear expert selection, out-of-bag probability calibration,
    stable neural weight transfer across changing input normalization,
    balanced class-wise undersampling with native sampling diagnostics,
    a single complementary soft ensemble for binary classification,
    a native C++ non-negative positive-unlabeled neural estimator,
    sensitivity analysis over prespecified class priors, bounded
    native C++ nonnegative-PU risk gradient residual regression trees
    with cross-fitted teachers and prior-robust holdout fallback, a matched
    same-network teacher ablation, an optional two-half verified-outcome
    gate for independently reserved trusted labels, and a
    label-uncertainty-guided resampling forest and a C++ class-mass-preserving
    stability sampler with constrained effective sample size, plus a
    fidelity-constrained model using the original nnPU network as a
    guaranteed exact fallback under unsuccessful inner selection, plus a
    strictly monotone C++ teacher-anchored forest distillation option, disjoint
    out-of-fold PU teacher predictions and validation-gated fallback,
    precision-recall surrogates and a separate inner validation split
    for early stopping of differentiable trees, preventing holdout reuse.
    Includes metric-driven model selection and phase-level training diagnostics,
    cross-validation, and transparent diagnostic and benchmarking functions.
    This is an experimental research implementation, not an established
    replacement for 'ranger'.
